WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.800
West Virginia, the Mountain State.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.800
It became the 35th state on June 20, 1863,
splitting from Virginia during the Civil War.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.800
Its official slogan is "Wild and Wonderful,"
and Spruce Knob, at 4,863 feet, is its highest point.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.800
The New River Gorge Bridge towers 876 feet above the river.
The gorge became a national park in 2020.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.800
At Green Bank, giant radio telescopes
operate inside the National Radio Quiet Zone.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.800
The state motto: Montani semper liberi.
Mountaineers are always free.
